    {
      "id": "claim_32e87fc15e0d4d0d99de8550036af6ea",
      "statement": "sessionTarget() implements double progression: with no prior performance it delegates to startingWeight()/recommend() at rep_min; a first working set below rep_min is treated as a load-calibration failure whose recalibrated target is capped at the previously logged load (never increased); reaching rep_max adds the exercise's increment and resets reps to rep_min; otherwise weight holds and target reps increase by one, and this bump test is reps-only (RIR feeds the e1RM estimate but never gates the bump).",
      "evidence": [
